<main>
<p>The Chords page lays out every diatonic chord of the current key across 8 or 12 pads, with a library of progressions to loop underneath whatever you're doing on the other pages.</p>

<h2>Chord Pads</h2>
<p>Pads 1–7 are the seven diatonic triads of the current key (I through vii°), coloured by root note. An 8th pad repeats the tonic an octave up. Switch to 12-pad mode to add the II–V chords an octave up as well.</p>

<h2>Key</h2>
<p>Choose any of the 12 keys and Major or Minor — the whole pad grid updates instantly to match.</p>

<h2>Chord Progressions</h2>
<p>A built-in library of progressions you can loop hands-free — Pop/Rock, Blues, 50s/Doo-wop, Jazz, Canon, Country/Folk, Anthem, Modern Pop, Gospel, Soul/R&amp;B in major, plus Rock minor, Classic minor vamp, Cinematic/Epic, Andalusian and Dramatic in minor.</p>
<ul class="guide">
  <li>Pick a progression and tap Play — it loops continuously</li>
  <li>Tap again to stop cleanly at the end of the current bar, never mid-chord</li>
  <li>Tap the BPM number to set the tempo</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip"><p>This is a library of ready-made progressions to play along to — recording your own performance is what the Melody Loops page's loop recorder is for.</p></div>

